---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Wallet: Expense & Budget Tracker Privacy Policy - Logicpath Systems">
    <section class="legal-page" style="padding-top: 120px; min-height: 100vh;">
        <div class="container reveal">
            <div class="glass-card" style="padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem);">
                <header style="margin-bottom: 3rem; text-align: center;">
                    <h1 class="gradient-text">Privacy Policy</h1>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;"><strong>Wallet: Expense &amp; Budget Tracker</strong></p>
                    <p style="color: var(--text-secondary);">Logicpath Systems &middot; <strong>Effective Date:</strong> November 6, 2026</p>
                </header>

                <main class="legal-content">
                    <p>This privacy policy applies to the Wallet: Expense &amp; Budget Tracker app (hereby referred to as &ldquo;Application&rdquo;) for mobile devices, created by Logicpath Systems (hereby referred to as &ldquo;Service Provider&rdquo;) as a free, ad-supported service. This service is intended for use &ldquo;AS IS&rdquo;.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>1. Summary</h2>
                    <p>Your financial data stays on your device. Transactions, amounts, categories, notes, budgets, accounts and imported statements are stored only in your device&rsquo;s local storage. The Service Provider never receives them.</p>
                    <p>The Application shows ads and uses analytics. To do this it uses Google AdMob and Google Analytics for Firebase, which collect some device and usage information as described in Section 4.</p>
                    <p>Your financial data is never shared with these services. No transaction amounts, categories, notes or statement contents are sent to AdMob, Firebase or any other third party.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>2. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
                    <p>All information you enter or import, including transactions, categories, amounts, notes, monthly budgets, accounts and their opening balances, and app settings, is saved only in your device&rsquo;s local storage.</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>PDF statement import:</strong> statements you choose to import are read and processed entirely on your device. The file and its contents are not uploaded anywhere. From each statement the Application keeps only what it needs: the date and time, amount, payee name, the UPI transaction reference (used to avoid importing the same payment twice) and your bank name with the last 2&ndash;4 digits of your account or card number (used to show balances per account). Full account or card numbers are never stored.</li>
                        <li><strong>Automatic categories:</strong> suggested categories for imported payments are worked out on your device, using built-in rules and the categories you chose before. Nothing is sent anywhere to do this.</li>
                        <li><strong>Reminders and budget alerts:</strong> these notifications are scheduled and calculated on your device. No server is involved.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The Service Provider has no access to this data and cannot view, recover or delete it on your behalf.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>3. Local Storage and Data Retention</h2>
                    <p>Because your financial data is stored locally:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>You have complete control over it.</li>
                        <li>If you uninstall the Application, clear the Application&rsquo;s data from your device settings, or lose your device, your data will be permanently deleted unless you have made a backup.</li>
                        <li>The Service Provider cannot recover lost data under any circumstances.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>4. Third-Party Services and the Data They Collect</h2>
                    <p>The Application uses the following third-party services, provided by Google LLC. These services collect information automatically and process it under their own privacy policies.</p>

                    <h3>Google AdMob (advertising)</h3>
                    <p>AdMob is used to show banner, full-screen, app open and rewarded video ads. To serve and measure ads, and to prevent fraud, AdMob may collect:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Your device&rsquo;s advertising ID (Android Advertising ID or Apple IDFA, where permitted)</li>
                        <li>Device information, such as device model, operating system version, language and screen size</li>
                        <li>Your IP address, which may be used to estimate your general location (country or city)</li>
                        <li>Ad interaction data, such as which ads were shown, clicked or watched</li>
                        <li>App diagnostics related to ad performance, such as crash and loading information</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>Ads may be personalised based on this information, depending on your consent choices and device settings (see Section 5).</p>

                    <h3>Google Analytics for Firebase (analytics)</h3>
                    <p>Firebase Analytics is used to understand how the Application is used, for example which screens are opened, so the Service Provider can improve it. It may collect:</p>
                    <ul>
                        <li>An app instance ID and device information, such as device model, operating system version and language</li>
                        <li>App usage data, such as screens viewed, session length, app opens and updates</li>
                        <li>Your IP address, which may be used to estimate your general location</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p>The Service Provider sees this information only in aggregated, non-identifying reports. Firebase Analytics does not receive your financial data.</p>

                    <h3>More information</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Google Privacy Policy: <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a></li>
                        <li>How Google uses information from apps that use its services: <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a></li>
                        <li>AdMob and user privacy: <a href="https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://support.google.com/admob/answer/6128543</a></li>
                        <li>Firebase privacy and security: <a href="https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);">https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy</a></li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>5. Your Choices</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Ad consent (EEA, UK and Switzerland):</strong> on first launch, you are asked for consent through Google&rsquo;s consent form before personalised ads or related data collection take place. You can change your choice at any time in Settings &rarr; Ad Privacy Choices.</li>
                        <li><strong>Personalised ads on Android:</strong> you can opt out of ads personalisation, or reset or delete your advertising ID, in your device settings (for example, Settings &rarr; Google &rarr; Ads, or Settings &rarr; Privacy &rarr; Ads, depending on your device).</li>
                        <li><strong>Personalised ads on iOS:</strong> you can limit ad tracking in Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; Security &rarr; Tracking.</li>
                        <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> you can turn daily reminders off in Settings &rarr; Daily Reminder, or block notifications in your device settings.</li>
                        <li><strong>Stop all collection:</strong> uninstalling the Application stops all further collection by the Application and its third-party services.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>6. Backups and Exports</h2>
                    <p>The Application lets you export your data as a JSON backup or CSV file, and share a summary image from Insights. These files are created locally on your device and are only shared when you choose to. If you choose to share or save them using another app (for example email or cloud storage), that app&rsquo;s privacy policy applies. It is your responsibility to store and manage backup files securely. The Service Provider has no access to your backups.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>7. Permissions Used</h2>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Internet / network access:</strong> to load ads and send analytics. Your financial data is never sent over the network by the Application.</li>
                        <li><strong>Advertising ID:</strong> to show and measure ads (see Section 4).</li>
                        <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> to show the daily reminder and budget alerts you choose to enable.</li>
                        <li><strong>Run at startup:</strong> so scheduled reminders still work after your device restarts.</li>
                        <li><strong>File access (only when you choose):</strong> to pick a PDF statement to import or a backup file to restore.</li>
                    </ul>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>8. Security</h2>
                    <p>Your financial data stays inside the secure sandbox provided by your device&rsquo;s operating system. However, no method of electronic storage is 100% secure, and the Service Provider cannot guarantee absolute security. We recommend protecting your device with a screen lock (PIN, password or biometrics).</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>9. Children&rsquo;s Privacy</h2>
                    <p>The Application is not directed at children under the age of 13, and the Service Provider does not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has provided information through the Application, please contact us using the details below.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>10. Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
                    <p>The Service Provider may update this Privacy Policy from time to time, for example when features or third-party services change. You are advised to review this page periodically. Changes are shown by updating the &ldquo;Effective Date&rdquo; at the top of this policy.</p>

                    <hr style="margin: 2.5rem 0; border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);" />

                    <h2>11. Contact Us</h2>
                    <p>If you have any questions or suggestions about this Privacy Policy, please contact us at:</p>
                    <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:contact@logicpathsystems.com" style="color: var(--accent-secondary);"><strong>contact@logicpathsystems.com</strong></a></p>
                </main>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</Layout>

<style>
    .legal-content h2 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 2.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 1rem;
        font-size: 1.5rem;
    }

    .legal-content h3 {
        color: var(--text-primary);
        margin-top: 1.5rem;
        margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
        font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .legal-content p, .legal-content ul {
        color: var(--text-secondary);
        margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
        font-size: 1.05rem;
        line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .legal-content ul {
        padding-left: 2rem;
        margin-bottom: 2rem;
    }

    .legal-content li {
        margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    }
</style>
